Here is an example of a React component that provides autocomplete functionality without relying on other third-party packages:
```
import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';

const Autocomplete = ({ suggestions, handleSelect }) => {
  const [inputValue, setInputValue] = useState('');
  const [activeSuggestion, setActiveSuggestion] = useState(-1);
  const [filteredSuggestions, setFilteredSuggestions] = useState([]);
  const [showSuggestions, setShowSuggestions] = useState(false);

  useEffect(() => {
    const onChangeText = (text) => {
      const filteredSuggestions = suggestions.filter((suggestion) => {
        return suggestion.toLowerCase().startsWith(text.toLowerCase());
      });
      setFilteredSuggestions(filteredSuggestions);
      setActiveSuggestion(-1);
    };
    const onKeyDown = (event) => {
      if (event.key === 'ArrowDown') {
        setActiveSuggestion(Math.min(activeSuggestion + 1, filteredSuggestions.length - 1));
      } else if (event.key === 'ArrowUp') {
        setActiveSuggestion(Math.max(activeSuggestion - 1, 0));
      } else if (event.key === 'Enter') {
        handleSelect(filteredSuggestions[activeSuggestion]);
      } else if (event.key === 'Escape') {
        setShowSuggestions(false);
      } else {
        onChangeText(inputValue);
      }
    };
    const onInputChange = (text) => {
      onChangeText(text);
      if (filteredSuggestions.length > 0) {
        setShowSuggestions(true);
      } else {
        setShowSuggestions(false);
      }
    };
    return () => {
      document.addEventListener('keydown', onKeyDown);
      document.addEventListener('input', onInputChange);
    };
  }, [activeSuggestion, filteredSuggestions, inputValue, suggestions]);

  const handleInput = (event) => {
    setInputValue(event.target.value);
  };

  return (
    <div>
      <input
        type="text"
        value={inputValue}
        onChange={handleInput}
        placeholder="Type to autocomplete"
      />
      {showSuggestions && (
        <ul>
          {filteredSuggestions.map((suggestion, index) => (
            <li
              key={index}
              className={
                activeSuggestion === index ? 'active-suggestion' : ''
              }
              onClick={() => handleSelect(suggestion)}
            >
              {suggestion}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      )}
    </div>
  );
};

export default Autocomplete;
```
This component accepts three props:

* `suggestions`: An array of suggestions that will be used for autocomplete
* `handleSelect`: A function that will be called when a suggestion is selected

The component uses the following state:

* `inputValue`: The current value of the input field
* `activeSuggestion`: The index of the currently active suggestion
* `filteredSuggestions`: An array of suggestions that match the current input value
* `showSuggestions`: A boolean indicating whether to show the suggestions list

The component uses the following effects:

* `useEffect` is used to set up event listeners for the input field and document. When the input field changes, the `onChangeText` function is called to filter the suggestions based on the current input value. When a key is pressed, the `onKeyDown` function is called to handle keyboard navigation and selection of suggestions.

